From a529ceec4af9ccae71aef9cb79a402808f1f1fa2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: e0358 <e0358@localhost>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:09:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add multi-user producer fusion and affine matmul to CUDA Tile
 IR translation

Affine loop fusion: profitable multi-user producer fusion (Asst-1).

mlir-translate --affine-to-cuda-tile translates a function of affine matmul
nests, c[i, j] += a[i, k] * b[k, j] with c zero-filled first, into a CUDA
Tile IR module with one kernel per group of matmuls; each kernel block
computes one tile of c, accumulating over k in f32. With
--cuda-tile-sibling-fusion, matmuls that read the same a (same shapes, and
none writing what another reads) share one kernel, which loads each tile of
a once for all of them.
